# reading 2 of boethius-foreknowledge.md by claude-opus-5-5
logic	s5
atom	foresees_all	God foresees everything (God knows all things)
atom	undeceivable	God can in no wise be deceived
atom	foreseen_occurs	that which providence foresees to be about to happen comes to pass
atom	free	there is freedom of the will
atom	sure_fk	there is sure foreknowledge of the future in God, not uncertain conjecture
# S2's "must necessarily come to pass" is read as metaphysical necessity, []
P1	S2	foresees_all ∧ undeceivable → □foreseen_occurs
# S3 calls providence "incapable of being deceived", which states undeceivable outright
P2	S3	undeceivable
# S3's "seeing that nothing can be done ... save such as providence has perceived" is read as: freedom requires that the foreseen could fail to happen
P3	S3	free → ◇¬foreseen_occurs
C1	S3	foresees_all → ¬free	from P1 P2 P3
P4	S4	◇¬foreseen_occurs → ¬sure_fk
# S4's "to think this of God I deem impiety" is taken as affirming that God has sure foreknowledge
P5	S4	sure_fk
C2	S4	□foreseen_occurs	from P4 P5
C	S1	¬(foresees_all ∧ free)	from C1
